<br/>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="weapons">Weapons for Protection Warrior Tank</h3>
<div class="pad"></div>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="main-hand-weapons-for-protection-warrior-tank">Main Hand Weapons for Protection Warrior Tank</h4>
<ul>
<li class="fa fa-arrow-right">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<i>While your choice of weapon was possibly the most intricate part of gearing a tank in previous expansions, with different speeds for different usage and preferred weapon types based on your talents, or race and unique weapon proficiencies, all of these nuances go out of the window with the new expansion. <b>In Cataclysm</b>, 99% of main-hands with strength are the same 2.60 speed tank-oriented weapons and the bonus expertise from <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=20597/sword-specialization">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_meleedamage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sword Specialization</span></a> or <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=20574/axe-specialization">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Axe Specialization</span></a> barely amount to a 1-2% TPS difference that we will mostly ignore to focus on better survivability since threat is no longer a concern.</i></div></li></ul>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=78488/souldrinker">
<img alt="Souldrinker" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_1h_deathwingraiddw_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Souldrinker</span></a> is pretty much the only weapon a <span class="c1">Protection</span> <a class="icontiny c1" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=1/warrior">
<img alt="Warrior" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warrior</span></a> cares about in Phase 4. It's the best tank weapon by a long shot thanks to its superior item level by virtue of being a <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=56173/deathwing">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Deathwing</span></a> drop with higher primary stats. Plus, it comes with a neat 15% chance to proc a <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=109831/drain-life">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_lifedrain02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Drain Life</span></a> effect which in itself contributes to 4% of your damage dealt and up to +1.5k HPS.<br/>
<br/>It's so good in fact that even its lower ilvl 390 version, which can be bought with <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3281/obsidian-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Obsidian Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Obsidian Fragment</span></span></a>s before even stepping into your first raid, is on par with other ilvl 410 one-handers from the <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5892/dragon-soul">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Dragon Soul</span></a> raid.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Weapon Enchants</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=74244/enchant-weapon-windwalk">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulasuperior_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Weapon - Windwalk</span></a>
<div class="pad"></div>
<div class="markup-table-wrapper">
<table class="grid max-width">
<tbody>
<tr>
